The weird thing about it is that it mixes two schemes: one that doesn't
attach any special meaning to 'c' and using it as a normal filesystem, 
and the other (that's very common in *BSD and Tru64) which uses c as 
a "whole disk" partition, thus indeed overlapping with everything else,
but of course it's not used to put a filesystem on.

Cheers,


Emile.

